  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1122 PM CDT MON AUG 17 2026\n\nOver the next several days, the upper-level ridge that has\ndominated the forecast will finally begin to slide west. While\nthis won't have an immediate effect on our afternoon highs\ntemperatures, it will allow for the region to come under the\ninfluence of a deep trough over the Midwest. Afternoon highs will\ngenerally start to decrease a degree or two here and there, with\ndew points slightly decreasing as well. Expect portions of the\nregion to remain in Heat Advisory criteria through at least\nWednesday, before heat index values drop once more into Friday.\n\nIt's during this timeframe that a few weak shortwaves should\nstart to clip this region, as the trough over the Midwest\ncontinues to deepen. More organized rain chances are possible\nFriday, and into the weekend, but confidence is currently low\nregarding overall coverage and rainfall amounts. With that being\nsaid, this deepening trough should allow for dry air to filter\nback into the region, dropping our peak heat index values well\nbelow heat advisory criteria through the weekend. However,\nafternoon highs will continue to reach the low to mid-90s, and\nwill likely stay here into early next week.\n\n/44/",
